{% comment %}
  Fills the EasyStore "Click ID" customer attribute, and hides it from shoppers.

  `attribution-click-id` has already stored the Cloudflare click id in the
  browser and exposed it as `window.ccSourceClickId`. This is the other half:
  putting that value somewhere EasyStore will keep, so the Contact sync can carry
  it to HubSpot as `easystore_attr_click_id` and the join script can resolve it
  against D1.

  A merchant-defined customer attribute is the only place a theme can write a
  fact onto a customer that the EasyStore API hands back. So the store defines one
  text attribute titled "Click ID", and this fills it during sign-up.

  **Included only by the four templates that render `shop.attribute_settings`**
  - `register`, `activate_account`, `details` and `account`. That is deliberate.
  An earlier version did this lookup from the layout head, which made every page
  in the store resolve a shop object that only the customer pages ask for, and
  the storefront errored on deploy. The lookup belongs on the pages that already
  do it.

  Three deliberate rules:

  * **Only ever filled when empty.** The cookie is last-touch - a shopper who
    comes back through a new link gets a new id - but the attribute records how
    the account was *acquired*, so once EasyStore holds a value nothing here
    overwrites it. `details` and `account` repopulate the field from
    `customer.attributes` while the page parses, so a value present by the time
    this runs is one EasyStore already recorded.
  * **The field is hidden, never removed.** Hiding it by id leaves the shared
    attribute loop untouched, so an admin who renames or deletes the attribute
    gets the ordinary field back rather than a broken form.
  * **A store with no such attribute is left completely alone.** No matching
    title means `attribution_click_id_setting` stays blank and everything below
    no-ops. The click id is still captured by the head snippet, so nothing is
    lost if the attribute is created later.

  Every filter chain here uses the same `default: '' | append: '' | downcase |
  strip` coercion the rest of the theme uses, and matches with `==` rather than
  testing an array with `contains`, which no other template in this theme does.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign attribution_click_id_setting = '' %}
{% for attribute_setting in shop.attribute_settings %}
  {% assign attribution_candidate_title = attribute_setting.title | default: '' | append: '' | downcase | strip %}
  {% if attribution_candidate_title == 'click id' or attribution_candidate_title == 'clickid' or attribution_candidate_title == 'cb_click_id' or attribution_candidate_title == 'source click id' or attribution_candidate_title == 'attribution click id' %}
    {% assign attribution_click_id_setting = attribute_setting.id %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if attribution_click_id_setting != '' %}
  {% comment %}
    Hidden before first paint. A shopper must never be shown a machine id in the
    middle of a sign-up form, and `:has()` reaches the wrapper that the shared
    attribute loop built, which a stylesheet on its own cannot.
  {% endcomment %}
  <style>
    .field:has(#DetailAttribute{{ attribution_click_id_setting }}),
    .grid__item:has(#DetailAttribute{{ attribution_click_id_setting }}) {
      display: none !important;
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    (function () {
      'use strict';

      var SETTING_ID = '{{ attribution_click_id_setting }}';

      function fill() {
        var field = document.getElementById('DetailAttribute' + SETTING_ID);
        if (!field) return;

        // Hidden by the stylesheet above; also hidden here so a browser lacking
        // :has() still never shows the field, and un-required so a required
        // attribute cannot block a sign-up on an invisible input. EasyStore may
        // enforce `is_required` server-side regardless, which is why the
        // attribute must not be marked required: an organic shopper has no click
        // id to fill.
        var wrapper = field.closest('.field, .grid__item');
        if (wrapper) {
          wrapper.setAttribute('hidden', 'hidden');
        }
        field.removeAttribute('required');

        var clickId = window.ccSourceClickId;
        if (!clickId) return;

        // Acquisition, not last touch: a value already here is one EasyStore
        // recorded when the account was created.
        if (!String(field.value || '').trim()) {
          field.value = clickId;
        }
      }

      if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', fill);
      } else {
        fill();
      }
    })();
  </script>
{% endif %}
